    "body": "## Purpose\nFirst visible VanDesign campervan-interior demonstration, built on the existing G3 cabinet/Fusion adapter and G4 branch. **Draft / not for merge yet.** One simplified envelope, rear bed platform, existing base cabinet as kitchen/storage, explicit placement and basic geometric fit checks.\n\n## Implementation\n- `demos/FirstInteriorDemo` manual Fusion script; refuses saved, modified or nonempty active documents. Does not save, close, switch or delete documents.\n- CAD-neutral `modules/interior_demo.py`: 1800 × 4000 × 2000 mm simplified envelope; rear bed deck nominal 1764 × 1900 mm at Z700; kitchen/storage cabinet 1200 × 850 × 550 mm offset X50/Y100; parametric bed length and kitchen offsets.\n- Fusion `cad/fusion/interior_demo.py`: actual BRep volume/bounds and stable-ID checks; intended cut emptiness and body interference checks; temporary Bed_Length 1900→1800 and Cab_Width 1200→1100 edits with finally-block restorations.\n- Does not change G3 geometry core, existing adapter, runner or protected designs.\n\n## Evidence and current state\n- **User's Fusion screenshot** showed new interior parts and Fusion popup **“Interior generated and verified”**, reporting local `demos/evidence/interior_20261015_005947.json`. This is **not yet an independently reviewed full JSON report**. Work should read the original local report and live runner inspect of the demo before declaring all stages PASS.\n- User confirmed 3/10 editable-document capacity; demo script run on a separately created empty, unsaved Fusion tab.\n- Offline demo tests 2 passed, foundation 5 passed.\n- Prototype regression suite ran 111 tests with **3 failures** in unchanged JSON fixtures attributed in recorded evidence to CRLF differences. This is **not a clean regression PASS**; investigate/triage before merge, avoid hiding these failures.\n- `demos/evidence/STATUS.md` and `demos/README.md` were authored before live demonstration; their UNKNOWN labels need updating only after reviewing real local report.\n- No van-specific measured fit, manufacturing readiness, furniture positioning UI or AI layout claimed.\n\n## Dependencies and safety\n**Base:** `feature/g4-safe-width-update` (draft PR #7). The stack also includes runner PR #6, G3 PR #5 and adapter PR #3. **Do not merge or retarget** without reviewed integration strategy.\n\n## Remaining acceptance for this demo\n1. Read and review original `interior_20261015_005947.json` for baseline, edit/restore stages, valid measurements, interference and stable IDs.\n2. Runner `inspect_design` confirms correct active demo document/managed components; preserve `v5-g3-tall` and other existing designs.\n3. Resolve/record three prototype regression failures and update status docs with evidence.\n4. Save the dedicated new demo only with user's approval; retain Fusion screenshot and evidence.",
